@@ -0,0 +1,20 @@
+## Context
+
+`src/index.ts` already has helpers `isObject`, `setOwn` (defineProperty, safe for `__proto__`) and `clone`, used by `applyPatch`. See proposal.md for motivation and scope.
+
+## Goals / Non-Goals
+
+- Goals: follow the RFC 7396 §2 algorithm exactly; never mutate inputs; be prototype-pollution safe.
+- Non-Goals: validation errors. Every JSON value is a valid patch, so the function does not throw for JSON input.
+
+## Decisions
+
+- Recursive implementation of the RFC pseudo-code: non-object patch → return a clone of the patch; otherwise start from a shallow copy of the target if it is an object, else `{}`; for each own key of the patch, `null` deletes, anything else sets `merge(targetMember, value)`. Recursing with the member (even a non-object) makes nulls in object patch values drop out, as the RFC specifies.
+- Build results with `setOwn` and delete via `delete` on own keys of fresh objects; iterate with `Object.keys` so inherited keys are ignored. Reuse `clone` for non-object patch values (alternative: share references — rejected, violates the no-shared-structure rule).
+- Result objects are plain `{}`; the target's key order is preserved, new keys are appended.
+- Recursion depth is bounded by input depth, same as `clone`; accepted.
+
+## Risks / Trade-offs
+
+- [RFC number in request is 7386] → Cite RFC 7396, which obsoletes it with identical semantics.
+- [Cannot set a member to `null`] → inherent to the standard; documented in the JSDoc.
