@@ -0,0 +1,21 @@
+## Why
+
+Some clients send partial updates as JSON Merge Patch documents rather than JSON Patch. The library offers `applyPatch` (RFC 6902) only, so services must hand-roll merge-patch handling, with a risk of getting `null`, array and `__proto__` handling wrong.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Add an exported `applyMergePatch(target, patch)` to `src/index.ts` that applies a JSON Merge Patch and returns the merged document as a new value.
+- Governing standard: JSON Merge Patch, RFC 7396 §2 (the `MergePatch` pseudo-code). The request cites "RFC 7386"; that is the original publication, which RFC 7396 obsoletes with the same algorithm, so RFC 7396 is cited (the project's own context also names RFC 7396).
+- Not breaking: purely additive; no existing export changes.
+- Out of scope: generating a merge patch from two documents, content-type / HTTP handling (RFC 7396 §3), and any change to `applyPatch`.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `json-merge-patch`: applying an RFC 7396 JSON Merge Patch to a JSON document.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+## Impact
+
+- `src/index.ts` (new export), new tests in `test/merge-patch.test.ts`. No dependency or `package.json` changes.
